---
description: PHP and Symfony bundle rules
globs:
  - "src/**/*.php"
  - "src/Resources/config/**/*.yaml"
  - ".symfony/recipe/**/*.yaml"
alwaysApply: false
---

Target this bundle compatibility by default: PHP >=8.2 <8.6 and Symfony 7.4 / 8.x (see `composer.json`).
Code must parse on PHP 8.2: write `(new Foo())->bar()`, never `new Foo()->bar()`.

Prefer:
- modern PHP with strict typing and explicit return types
- PSR-12 coding style (`make cs-check` / `make cs-fix`)
- final classes by default, readonly where appropriate
- constructor injection; PSR-20 `Psr\Clock\ClockInterface` for time and PSR-3 `Psr\Log\LoggerInterface` for logs (see `docs/PSR.md`)
- small focused services (`src/GoogleWallet`, `src/AppleWallet`, `src/Service`, `src/Twig`)
- keeping `NowoWalletQrExtension`, `Configuration` and the Twig functions backward compatible
- an English PHPDoc block on every public class and public method in `src/`
- never logging private keys, JWTs, save URLs or pass payloads

Before finishing a PHP change run `make cs-check`, `make phpstan`, `make rector-dry` and `make test`.

Do not introduce BC breaks unless explicitly requested.
Do not rename public services, configuration keys, or Twig functions without a deprecation path.
Do not touch unrelated namespaces or files.
